= Conditional probability — Technical =

== Event conditioning ==
For P(B)>0:

<pre>
P(A|B)=P(A∩B)/P(B)
</pre>

This defines a new probability measure over A for fixed B.

== Chain rule ==
Repeated conditioning gives:

<pre>
P(A₁,...,Aₙ)
= Πᵢ P(Aᵢ | A₁,...,Aᵢ₋₁)
</pre>

for a compatible ordering.

== Law of total probability ==
For partition {Bᵢ}:

<pre>
P(A)=Σᵢ P(A|Bᵢ)P(Bᵢ)
</pre>

which supplies the denominator in many applications of Bayes' theorem.

== Measure-zero conditioning ==
For continuous variables, conditioning on exact values often requires regular conditional distributions rather than the elementary ratio definition.

== Causal contrast ==
Observational conditioning:

<pre>
P(Y|X=x)
</pre>

differs conceptually from interventional quantities such as:

<pre>
P(Y|do(X=x))
</pre>

in causal modeling.

